And I would make one further architectural rule explicit:

A Target Packet must never manufacture a new lens vocabulary merely because the scope changed.

If Surface OWNERSHIP has five meaningful analytical dimensions, Target Packet OWNERSHIP should inherit those dimensions. The packet supplies the micro evidence, interpretation, unresolved conditions, and sharpening inputs for the searched subject.

That makes the packet genuinely feel like going deeper into the same intelligence, rather than navigating to an entirely different analytical product.

And it explains why your instinct about the current STAKE / MOVE / WINDOW / LEVERAGE FIELD was correct: those aren't necessarily bad concepts, but they are not the reusable lens intelligence you already built. They are an intervening template.

The cleaner architecture is:

Capture once → scope repeatedly → synthesize afterward.

